  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the maintainer of the MPStorage flows, I want real captures of a private message whose subject is the MPStorage subject but which another member started, so that #1200 P1's handling of such a thread rests on captured pages instead of a page derived from `R60a`.\n\n### Context\n\n#1200 P1 (PR #1202) makes the MP list hide only the account's own storage thread, and the storage search skip a storage-subject thread whose first message is not the account's. That rule rests on verified facts (no edit link on another member's post: `RU1`, `R44`, `R63a`; the storage row names the recipient as interlocutor: `R13u1`, `R13u1b`, `R333b`). But no capture shows such a foreign thread itself. The transport test derives its page from `R60a` minus the edit links (`MPStorageCapture.threadPageOfAnotherMember`), which LESSONS 36 says to replace with a capture (Fable review round 1 on #1202, finding 4).\n\n### What to capture (kit accounts only, anonymized per FIXTURES.md)\n\n1. user2 sends user1 a new MP whose subject is exactly `a2bcc09b796b8c6fab77058ff8446c34` (the public constant `MP_NAME`), with a plain text body.\n2. As user1: the MP list page holding that row (before opening it), with the row's interlocutor and `[non lu]` marker as served.\n3. As user1: the thread's first page (`/forum2.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=prive&post=<post>&numreponse=0&page=1&p=1&subcat=0&sondage=0&owntopic=0`, the URL the storage search GETs): its toolbar, with no edit link expected.\n4. As user1: the MP list again right after that GET, to see whether the GET alone marked the thread read for user1.\n5. Clean up: delete the thread from both accounts.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- The captures and their `.meta.json` are committed and pass the anonymization check.\n- `MPStorageTransportReadTests.skipsForeignThreadWithStorageSubject` reads the captured page instead of the derived one, and `MPStorageThreadHidingTests` gets a captured foreign row.\n- HFR-PROTOCOL §6c (LOT-038 storage row) records what step 4 showed.\n\nRefs #1200, #1202.",
