   "body": "**cloud/i1200-opus**: one more question for this capture run, from Fable's round 2 on #1202 (nit 7).\n\n`PrivateMessageListPage.hidingStorageThread` hides a one-to-one storage-subject thread whose interlocutor matches the storage recipient `MultiMP`, compared through `HFRText.pseudoComparisonKey`, which lower-cases. Nothing captured shows that HFR pseudos are unique regardless of case. If they are not, a member named `multimp` could send a storage-subject MP that the list would hide.\n\nTo capture or cite: whether HFR refuses to register a pseudo that differs from an existing one only by case (registration form answer, or a documented source). If case-distinct pseudos can exist, the comparison should be case-sensitive (`normalizedPseudo` only), and a follow-up should change it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
